id: pm-9yhl2v
title: Unsupported assurance triggers bypass the typed evaluation-refusal boundary and surface as high-severity Sentry faults
description: "evaluateAssuranceGate throws a raw TypeError when a named gate does not declare the requested lifecycle trigger. The CLI action already normalizes AssuranceEvaluationRefusalError into a stable usage refusal, so this single raw branch becomes unclassified_runtime_error telemetry and a high-severity handled Sentry fault instead of actionable user guidance."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-13T11:58:14.430Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-14T02:03:02.547Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-14T02:00:05.601Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-14T02:00:05.601Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: The SDK preserves TypeError compatibility through AssuranceEvaluationRefusalError while CLI and MCP transports receive a PmCliError usage refusal.; Focused SDK and CLI regression tests prove the exact undeclared-trigger path is typed and normalized.; The fresh Sentry release gate finding is documented and publication remains fail-closed until the immutable next release contains the correction.
parent: pm-1jzupz
release: 2026.8.14
severity: high
resolution: "Missing gates and undeclared lifecycle triggers now throw AssuranceEvaluationRefusalError, preserving TypeError compatibility for SDK callers while normalizing CLI and MCP transports to stable invalid_argument_value guidance."
expected_result: Unsupported gate triggers return a structured invalid_argument_value assurance_evaluation_refused usage response and are excluded from unexpected-fault Sentry reporting.
actual_result: PM-CLI-33 recorded a handled high-priority TypeError for tracker-context-quality with trigger pre-commit on pm-cli@2026.8.13.
fixed_version: 2026.8.14
component: SDK assurance evaluation
regression: true
